# CICD-CTRL-1 — Safe CI Runtime Control

CI gate selection is decided by the conservative classifier
`scripts/ci/resolve-gates.sh` and governed by `config/ci_runtime_control.php`.

Non-negotiable rules:

- **DEFAULT-STRONG.** Any uncertainty (no diff, unreachable base, unknown path)
  resolves to `unknown_high_risk` → every gate runs.
- **`docs_only` is the ONLY profile that may skip the critical Pest step.**
  Every changed file must be Markdown for `docs_only`. Any code, config,
  workflow, script, dependency, test, migration, route, policy, permission, or
  view change forces the critical gate. Do not widen `skip_critical_profiles`
  without a reviewed sprint + tests.
- **Always-on gates.** `quality_gate`, `release_safety_gate` (NSF-9), and
  `nsf10_release_evidence_gate` are never gated by the classifier. Security,
  governance, release-safety, evidence, and smoke gates always run.
- **Full-suite fallback preserved.** The full Pest suite stays available via
  schedule (weekly), manual dispatch, and push-to-base. Do not delete it.
- **No unsafe path filtering.** Never add `paths-ignore` or blanket path filters
  to the workflow; selection is the audited classifier, not opaque globs.
- **Additive only.** Module flags add module test coverage; they never downgrade
  the critical gate.

Verify with `php artisan foundation:ci-runtime-control-check --strict`
(re-verifies the ENT-10 enterprise gate stays GO). Preview locally with
`scripts/ci/resolve-gates.sh --base origin/<base> --head HEAD`.
